#: includes/diagnostics.php:166
msgid "There is no SPF record"
msgstr ""

#: includes/diagnostics.php:166
msgid "Receivers have no way to know which servers may send mail for this domain, and most of them treat that as a bad sign. Publish a TXT record starting with v=spf1 that lists your provider and ends with -all."
msgstr ""

#: includes/diagnostics.php:169
msgid "The SPF record is invalid"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: number of lookups
#: includes/diagnostics.php:177
#, php-format
msgid "SPF uses %d DNS lookups; the limit is 10"
msgstr ""

#: includes/diagnostics.php:178
msgid "Going over the limit does not degrade SPF gracefully: receivers return a permanent error and the whole record stops counting, as if it did not exist. Remove providers you no longer use, or replace include: entries with ip4: entries where the provider documents stable addresses."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: number of lookups
#: includes/diagnostics.php:185
#: includes/diagnostics.php:193
#, php-format
msgid "SPF uses %d of the 10 allowed DNS lookups"
msgstr ""

#: includes/diagnostics.php:186
msgid "One more provider and it will break. Look at the tree below for includes you can remove."
msgstr ""

#: includes/diagnostics.php:194
msgid "Within the limit."
msgstr ""

#: includes/diagnostics.php:199
msgid "SPF ends with +all"
msgstr ""

#: includes/diagnostics.php:199
msgid "That authorises every server on the internet to send as this domain. It is the same as having no SPF, and worse in the eyes of most receivers. Change it to -all."
msgstr ""

#: includes/diagnostics.php:201
msgid "SPF does not end with -all or ~all"
msgstr ""

#: includes/diagnostics.php:201
msgid "Without a failing qualifier at the end, mail from unlisted servers is neither accepted nor rejected — receivers treat the record as saying nothing. Use -all once you are sure every legitimate sender is listed, or ~all while you check."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: provider name
#: includes/diagnostics.php:218
#, php-format
msgid "%s is not authorised in the SPF record"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: provider name, 2: include to add
#: includes/diagnostics.php:221
#, php-format
msgid "This site sends through %1$s, but the SPF record does not include it, so receivers will see the mail as coming from an unauthorised server. Add include:%2$s to the record."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: provider name
#: includes/diagnostics.php:235
#, php-format
msgid "SPF authorises %s, which is not the configured transport"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: include
#: includes/diagnostics.php:238
#, php-format
msgid "If nothing else on this domain sends through it any more, remove include:%s — it spends one of the 10 lookups and lets that provider send as you. If another system still uses it, leave it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/diagnostics.php:253
msgid "No DKIM selector was found"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: number of selectors probed
#: includes/diagnostics.php:256
#, php-format
msgid "None of the %d selectors probed exists on this domain. That does not prove there is no DKIM — selectors cannot be listed over DNS, only guessed — but if your provider gave you DKIM records to publish and they are not here, mail is going out unsigned. Add your provider's selector in the settings and revalidate."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: selector
#: includes/diagnostics.php:267
#, php-format
msgid "Selector %s is revoked"
msgstr ""

#: includes/diagnostics.php:268
msgid "It exists but carries an empty key, which is the standard way of saying \"this key no longer signs anything\". If your provider uses it, mail is going out with a signature nobody can verify."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: selector
#: includes/diagnostics.php:275
#, php-format
msgid "Selector %s uses a 1024-bit key"
msgstr ""

#: includes/diagnostics.php:276
msgid "It works, but 1024 bits is considered weak and some receivers score it down. Most providers can rotate to 2048 from their dashboard."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: selector, 2: key size
#: includes/diagnostics.php:283
#, php-format
msgid "Selector %1$s is published (%2$s)"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: selector, 2: key size
#: includes/diagnostics.php:283
msgid "key size unknown"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: CNAME target
#: includes/diagnostics.php:286
#, php-format
msgid "Delegated by CNAME to %s, so the provider rotates the key for you."
msgstr ""

#: includes/diagnostics.php:287
msgid "Published directly on the domain."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: provider name
#: includes/diagnostics.php:307
#, php-format
msgid "No DKIM record for %s"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: provider name, 2: selectors
#: includes/diagnostics.php:310
#, php-format
msgid "%1$s signs mail with the selector(s) %2$s, and none of them is published on this domain. Mail goes out signed by the provider's own domain instead of yours, which does not count for DMARC alignment. Copy the DKIM records from the provider's dashboard into your DNS."
msgstr ""

#: includes/diagnostics.php:319
msgid "There is no DMARC record"
msgstr ""

#: includes/diagnostics.php:319
msgid "Without DMARC, receivers decide on their own what to do when SPF and DKIM do not add up, and you get no reports about who is sending as your domain. Start with v=DMARC1; p=none; rua=mailto:you@yourdomain to receive reports without affecting delivery, then tighten it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/diagnostics.php:322
msgid "The DMARC record is invalid"
msgstr ""

#: includes/diagnostics.php:328
msgid "DMARC policy is p=none: monitoring only"
msgstr ""

#: includes/diagnostics.php:328
msgid "Receivers report but do nothing. It is the right first step; once the reports show only legitimate senders, move to p=quarantine."
msgstr ""

#: includes/diagnostics.php:330
msgid "rejected"
msgstr ""

#: includes/diagnostics.php:330
msgid "sent to spam"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: policy
#: includes/diagnostics.php:337
#, php-format
msgid "DMARC policy is p=%s: alignment is required"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: what happens to the mail
#: includes/diagnostics.php:340
#, php-format
msgid "Mail that fails both SPF and DKIM alignment will be %s. With no transport configured here, this plugin cannot tell whether your sender aligns."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: policy
#: includes/diagnostics.php:349
#, php-format
msgid "DMARC policy is p=%s and mail aligns through DKIM"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: provider name
#: includes/diagnostics.php:352
#, php-format
msgid "SPF alignment usually fails with a third-party provider — the bounce address is theirs, not yours — but %s signs with your domain's DKIM key, and one aligned mechanism is enough."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: policy
#: includes/diagnostics.php:361
#, php-format
msgid "DMARC policy is p=%s but nothing aligns"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: provider name, 2: what happens to the mail
#: includes/diagnostics.php:364
#, php-format
msgid "With %1$s as the transport, SPF is not aligned (the bounce address belongs to the provider) and no DKIM key of yours is published for it. Every message will be %2$s. Publish the provider's DKIM records — that is the fix — or drop the policy to p=none until you do."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: percentage
#: includes/diagnostics.php:377
#, php-format
msgid "The policy applies to %d%% of mail"
msgstr ""

#: includes/diagnostics.php:378
msgid "pct= below 100 means receivers apply the policy to a sample and let the rest through. Fine while ramping up; set it to 100 when you are done."
msgstr ""

#: includes/diagnostics.php:383
msgid "DMARC has no report address (rua)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/diagnostics.php:383
msgid "You will never learn who is sending as your domain or what fails. Add rua=mailto:an-address-you-read."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: address
#: includes/diagnostics.php:392
#, php-format
msgid "Reports to %s are being discarded"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: report domain, 2: name of the missing record
#: includes/diagnostics.php:395
#, php-format
msgid "That address is on another domain (%1$s), and the standard requires that domain to say it accepts reports for yours. It does not: there is no TXT record at %2$s with v=DMARC1. Until it is published, receivers throw the reports away."
msgstr ""

#: includes/diagnostics.php:406
msgid "The domain has no MX record"
msgstr ""

#: includes/diagnostics.php:406
msgid "Sending still works, but nothing can be received at this domain: replies and bounces to your From address go nowhere, and some receivers distrust senders that cannot receive."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: host, 2: target
#: includes/diagnostics.php:414
#, php-format
msgid "Return-path %1$s points to %2$s"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: host, 2: target
#: includes/diagnostics.php:414
msgid "The provider's custom bounce domain is set up, so SPF can align too."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: host
#: includes/diagnostics.php:416
#, php-format
msgid "Return-path %s does not resolve"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: host
#: includes/diagnostics.php:416
msgid "The provider offers a custom bounce domain that makes SPF align with your domain. It is optional — DKIM alignment is enough for DMARC — but publishing the CNAME the provider gives you improves reputation."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: provider name
#: includes/diagnostics.php:475
#, php-format
msgid "%s does not look set up for this domain"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: provider name, 2: the domain
#: includes/diagnostics.php:478
#, php-format
msgid "Neither %1$s's SPF include nor any of its DKIM selectors is published for %2$s, which is what a domain that was never added on their side looks like. Providers refuse mail from a domain they have not verified, so this is not about landing in spam: the message does not leave at all, and what comes back is a number. Add the domain in your account there, publish the DNS records it gives you, and wait for it to read as verified before looking at anything else on this screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/dns-dmarc.php:67
msgid "There is more than one DMARC record. Receivers ignore all of them when that happens."
msgstr ""

#: includes/dns-dmarc.php:92
msgid "The record has no policy (p=). Without it the record is invalid and receivers ignore it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/dns-spf.php:51
msgid "The domain publishes more than one SPF record. The standard treats that as a permanent error: receivers ignore all of them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/dns-spf.php:146
msgid "Already included above: this is a loop."
msgstr ""

#: includes/dns-spf.php:168
msgid "No SPF record. An include that leads nowhere still counts as a lookup, and too many of these are an error on their own."
msgstr ""

#: includes/dns.php:246
msgid "The DNS could not be queried: dns_get_record() is unavailable and the DNS-over-HTTPS resolver did not answer."
msgstr ""

